2.5.2 Characterization
The characterization of the spray has been operated for both fuels, for the three
atomizer configurations and in conditions of both aligned and misaligned nozzles.
In conditions of nozzle misalignment, the direction of the liquid columns is
translated on the horizontal plane, in order to avoid their impingement. The applied
misalignment is the minimal required for avoid the impact, in the attempt to isolate
the effects of the collision with the smallest modification of the geometrical
configuration.
Each injector head configuration have been investigated on three different values of
fuel flow rate ṁF, and on six different values of air flow rate ṁA, as described in Table
2.3 and Table 2.4.
The ṁF values differ for the two fuels, as the flow rates have been controlled through
the same rotameter, and the two fuels affect the rotameter in a different manner
(because of their different densities).
The conditions of lower ṁA have not been investigated in misaligned conditions in
order to avoid the soiling of the receiver optics, as the defect of air results in an
uncomplete fragmentation of the liquid columns, which proceed undisturbed on
their misaligned direction. In these cases the characterization has been extended to
ṁA = 0.44 g/s, in order to keep a sufficient data size for the description of the
behaviour in the specific conditions.


